A||||18||Spektyr||Shifter Woes||||5||
Z||000000||Spektyr||04-17-2001||12:45 PM||||Okay, I'm a shade-tree mechanic, but I've never been under the hood of a Fiero before.  My friend owns one and he tells me he's just lost 1st, 3rd, and 5th gears.  2nd, 4th and reverse still work.  My gut tells me this is probably a linkage problem since all of the broken gears are forward throws.  If it helps in the diagnosis, he let another friend of his drive the car and it came back broken.  (this particular person I wouldn't trust to take care of my pet rock...)<P>Am I right that this is just a linkage problem, or is there a rather costly repair in this car's future?  I apologize for the lack of information on the problem, I haven't had a chance to look at the car yet.<P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Johnson's85SE||04-17-2001||12:59 PM||||Hey, <BR> Aren't we all shady tree~. Tell him to check the two adjustment cables above the transmission case. One cable controls, side to side movment, while the other controls up and down. One of them might have came loose. <BR>or is just misaligned. Cheers!<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Taijiguy||04-17-2001||12:59 PM||||It does look like a linkage thing, since they are all gears that are on the forward throw of the shifter (which would be moving the shifter arm on the trans towards the back of the car. It's possible the cable has moved on the arm so that it won't go far enough back to engage those gears. 15mm socket to make the adjustments.<BR>~Taiji<p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DerekD||04-17-2001||01:34 PM||||Almost Garranteed its the cables that have broken, I lost the exact gears last summer when two cables decided to give in on me.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Drive It Like You Stole IT !||||reg||9
Z||000004||85seNUT||04-17-2001||02:39 PM||||the same thing happened to me with 1st and 3rd(4 spd).  i took it down and had to get the upper thow cable replaced because of some black little cover that was on the cable kept slipping downward everytime i was attempting to put it into gear.  i dont know if that heps but thats the lamons version.  =)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spektyr||04-18-2001||12:56 PM||||Okay, so adjust or replace the cable.  That sounds relatively easy.  Do those that have done this have any advice on the proceedure?<P>Seems I should just have to put it on jack stands, and then either adjust or replace the cable.  (I'll probably end up getting the Haynes manual as well.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spektyr||04-18-2001||09:37 PM||||Anyone?  Please?<P>Looks like I'll be working on the car tomorrow and I'd really appreciate any advice anyone can give me on this job.  The manuals are helpful, but there's no substitute for first hand knowledge.<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektyr||04-19-2001||04:27 PM||||Bump||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||04-19-2001||05:58 PM||||My 85SE v-6 4spd cables are accessed from the top.  No need to jack the car up.  I believe this is the case with the 5 spd also.<P>The Haynes manual should have the procedure for replacing/adjusting the cables.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000009||GodSend||04-19-2001||07:07 PM||||Just a tip,<P> You wont find much under the hood! Check under the rear deck lid.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Spektyr||04-19-2001||10:09 PM||||Turns out the C-clip on the transmission end was gone.  The parts store didn't have a Fiero C-clip, but they had a standard one that fit, so I've got all my gears now.<P>Amazingly easy to drive with just 2nd and 4th, DEFINITELY much quicker with 1st and 3rd working.  And reverse is rather helpful too.<P>Not too bad for a car I paid $100 bucks for...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Spektyr||04-19-2001||10:09 PM||||Turns out the C-clip on the transmission end was gone.  The parts store didn't have a Fiero C-clip, but they had a standard one that fit, so I've got all my gears now.<P>Amazingly easy to drive with just 2nd and 4th, DEFINITELY much quicker with 1st and 3rd working.  And reverse is rather helpful too.<P>Not too bad for a car I paid $100 bucks for...||||reg||6
