Z||000014||Spektyr||04-20-2001||12:28 AM||||Yup, you heard right.  1985 V6 GT for 100 bucks.<P>Bought it from a friend who recently bought a '93 Caprice Police Interceptor.  He was tired of the Fiero breaking down on him (not mechanically inclined this guy).<P>He was willing to just give me the car if I'd get it out of his driveway, but I just couldn't do that to a friend.  I mean the C-clip didn't cost me anything.  So far I've spent about 80 bucks on seat covers, floor mats, an oil cap that doesn't fit and the Haynes manual.<P>I had to give him a hundred so I didn't feel like I was stealing the car.  hehe||||reg||1
Z||000015||thomas_l||04-20-2001||12:00 PM||||Some people have all the luck. I paid $500 for mine including title transfer & tow to my house. Transmission not included...<P>At least everything is working except the RH headlamp and that's just missing a $0.05 pin bushing and lamp.||||reg||8
Z||000016||Spektyr||04-20-2001||02:12 PM||||Well, if it makes you feel better, the headliner is shredded, the leather shift handle is worn through, it's missing the oil filler cap, and I have to pop the hood and hotwire my right side headlight if I want it to go up or down.<P>Of course I've already ordered a replacement oil cap and shift handle, and I'm an ex-Navy electronics technician, so I can probably fix the headlamp if I decide not to just replace it.<P>But the paint is badly oxidized, and painting is NOT a skill I want to learn by practicing on this car.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
Z||000017||thomas_l||04-20-2001||03:58 PM||||Hehe... OK I feel better now. Mine isn't in too bad a shape all things considered. Now that I'm running, this weekend will be a trip to the muffler shop for a new cat for passing smog inspection. My wife has advised some time with the steam cleaner to get the mildew odor out too. I think mine was parked outdoors with the drivers window down for several months. The shop vac got most of the filth, but it needs soap too.||||reg||10
Z||000018||Spektyr||04-20-2001||04:30 PM||||Hehe, sounds like my interior... needs a thorough flogging with a vacuum, and it wouldn't hurt to clean the vinyl.<P>I have half a mind to simply strip most of the interior out to do it.  I'd get it a lot more clean that way...<P>Maybe in a week or two, it's just too much fun to drive to take it apart right now.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
